This extension adds Doom I & II (UZDoom) modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Automatically installs DML and UZDoom and checks for updates.[/summary]

[color=#ffff00][size=3][b]This extension will automatically download and install [url=https://github.com/Premo36/DML2.X]DML[/url] and [url=https://github.com/UZDoom/UZDoom]UZDoom[/url] for the user. This extension is built on top of these open-source software packages. Vortex checks for DML and UZDoom updates when Vortex runs an update check
[color=#f6b26b][size=3][b]Note: Game WADs (DOOM.WAD and DOOM2.WAD) must be obtained by the user and installed as a mod in Vortex. The WADs cannot be included here for legal reasons.[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*][size=2]If you own DOOM 3: BFG Edition or DOOM Eternal, WADs are included in their game files ("base/wads" and "base/classicwads", respectively).[/size][/*]
[/list]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Doom Mod Loader installs to the "DML" folder.[/*]
[*]UZDoom mods with a "uzdoom.exe" file install to the "DML\FILE\PORT\gzdoom" folder.[/*]
[*]IWAD (Game) mods with a "doom.wad", "doom2.wad", "freedoom.wad" or "nerve.wad" file and a ".iwad" or ".ipk3" file install to the "DML\FILE\IWAD" folder.[/*]
[*]Mods with a ".wad", ".pk3", ".zip", ".pak", ".pk7", ".grp" or one of 4 other file types install to the "DML\FILE\PWAD" folder.[/*]
[*]Nested Archive mods are supported.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Installs mods (".wad", ".pk3", ".zip", ".pak", ".pk7", ".grp", ".rff", ".deh", ".iwad", ".ipk3") for UZDoom to the correct folder for DML to detect them automatically.[/*]
[*]Installs game wads ("IWADs") to the correct folder for DML to detect them automatically.[/*]
[*][size=2]There is no restriction on what folder you choose for installation. Everything will be contained with a top level folder for DML, but please be mindful to select a sensible installation folder where your Windows user account has write access.[/size][/*]
[*][size=2]The user must configure DML after launching the first time.[/size][/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Doom I & II (UZDoom) mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Doom Mod Loader:

Handled by the "testDML" installer. Inspect the extension source for the exact archive layout it expects.

  Installs to: "DML"

========================================================================

UZDoom:

Recognised when the archive contains a "uzdoom.exe" file.

  Installs to: "DML\FILE\PORT\gzdoom"

========================================================================

IWAD (Game):

Recognised when the archive contains a "doom.wad", "doom2.wad", "freedoom.wad" or "nerve.wad" file and a ".iwad" or ".ipk3" file.

  Installs to: "DML\FILE\IWAD"

========================================================================

Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".wad", ".pk3", ".zip", ".pak", ".pk7", ".grp", ".rff", ".deh", ".iwad" or ".ipk3" file.

  Installs to: "DML\FILE\PWAD"

========================================================================

Zip Mod:

Handled by the "testZipContent" installer. Inspect the extension source for the exact archive layout it expects.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

